# The three products' binaries.
slim-vim
whim-vim
zero-vim

# The upper part of zero-vim.c on its own -- the core editor, cut at the first
# #include, which is the boundary.  Produced by `make editor.c`, never edited; it
# is a prefix of a tracked file and git already has every byte of it.
editor.c

# The frozen snapshot of this tree, plus the harness baselines.  Data, and a
# copy of what git already has -- not source.  See CLAUDE.md.
.reference/

# The exported session transcript, written by /export whenever CLAUDE.md is
# updated.  Half a megabyte of conversation; the reasoning that matters is in
# the commit messages.
TRANSCRIPT.md

# The pristine vim trees the makefile clones in for a pass and deletes after --
# the fast path's, and the reference path's.  8,581 files that must never reach
# a commit.  See SLIM-GOAL.md.
upstream/
upstream-ref/

# What a pass leaves behind: phase snapshots, boundary digests, per-phase agent
# streams and timings.  .build-slim/ is a restore point and a development asset
# -- converting a phase to a program means restoring the previous boundary and
# comparing the next -- but it is data, not source, and a new pass discards it.
.build-slim/
.build-whim/
.build-zero/

# The whim pipeline's work directory: one file and a makefile, rebuilt from
# slim-vim.c on demand and deleted with the build.  zero/ is the same, from whim-vim.c.
whim/
zero/

# Tier 3 of the memoize: phase results, keyed by input digest and
# implementation digest together.  Pure cache -- content-keyed, so it cannot go
# stale, and deleting it costs only the time to recompute.  Since the Go
# cutover it also holds what tools/gobuild.sh composes: gobin/ (the slimtools
# binary, keyed on every file under tools/go plus go.mod, go.sum and the cc/v4
# patch) and gofork/ (the pinned cc/v4 module with that patch applied).  Both
# are content-keyed the same way and rebuild from the local Go module cache,
# measured with GOPROXY=off, so `make clean-cache` needs no network.
.cache/

# The transient insight log, folded into SLIM-GOAL.md and CLAUDE.md and then deleted.
PROGRESS.md

# Editing this tree with the editor it builds.  Vim names the FIRST swap file
# .swp and then walks backwards -- .swo, .swn, .swm and on down -- so a second
# session on the same file, or a crashed one, leaves a name this pattern has to
# cover.  Naming only *.swp left .swn and .swo untracked-but-reported in the
# root, which is how this was noticed.
*.sw[a-p]

# Python leaves these beside tools/.
__pycache__/
*.pyc

# Claude Code's per-project directory.
.claude/
